-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",311,{
[9921]="70025EAB\n1\tPull weeds (total: 12)\tThe weeds are around the market area at the Northcotton Farm. Milo Longfurrow asked you to pull some weeds around the market area.\n2\tTalk to Milo Longfurrow\tMilo Longfurrow is at the Northcotton Farm. Milo Longfurrow will be pleased to hear that the weeds have been pulled.\n",
[9922]="700272B0\n1\tDefeat Draig-lûth at Uvel-cadlus (total: 10)\tDraig-lûth can be found in Uvel-cadlus. Thurbald has asked you to defeat several Dragon-clan warriors.\n2\tTalk to Thurbald\tThurbald is hiding to the south of Uvel-cadlus. You should return to Thurbald with news of your victory.\n",
[9923]="700598EA\n1\tDefeat half-orc poachers (total: 3)\tThe poachers' camp can be found in the southern Wildwood. The hunter has asked for your assistance in defeating the poachers who trapped him.\n2\tTalk to the hunter\tThe hunter can be found in the western Wildwood. You should talk to the hunter you freed.\n",
[9924]="7003FFBF\n1\tDefeat looters (total: 4)\tThe looters must be defeated.\n",
[9925]="7002720B\n1\tDefeat Prudwen's guards (total: 4)\030Find Prudwen Brehur at his home and confront him\tPrudwen Brehur may be found at his home in Upper Barnavon.\n2\tTalk to Lunwen in Barnavon\tLunwen is at the centre of Lower Barnavon. You should return to Lunwen with news of Prudwen's defeat.\n",
[9926]="70041172\n1\tDefeat Umbarrim in Tarlang's Crown (total: 4)\tThe Umbarrim can be found throughout Tarlang's Crown, especially in the central camp. You have encountered the Umbarrim and should defeat them, lest their might be used against Gondor.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many Umbarrim in Tarlang's Crown.\n",
[9927]="7001A49E\n1\tDestroy the idol of the Necromancer\tThe idol of the Necromancer can be found in Burgûl-stazg, north-west from Echad Mothelen. Mothelen has instructed you to find and destroy the idol of the Necromancer.\n2\tTalk to Mothelen at Echad Mothelen\tMothelen is at Echad Mothelen, south-east from Burgûl-stazg. You should return to Mothelen with news of your success.\n",
[9928]="70032162\n1\tDefeat wights within the ancient tomb (total: 15)\030Defeat bats and rats within the ancient tomb (total: 25)\tThe ancient tomb can be found in the eastern section of the Norcrofts, just south of Elthengels. The inhabitants of the crypt must be dealt with to restore the deserving tranquility of those entombed.\n2\tComplete\tYou have defeated many of the hostile inhabitants of the ancient tomb. In time, peace and order may be restored to this once calm resting place.\n",
[9929]="700370A2\n1\tDefeat marsh-slugs\tWhile you are hunting for the leader of the brigands, you might assist the people of Oserley by clearing the poisonous slugs out of the marshes.\n2\tDefeat marsh-slugs (total: 10)\tMarsh-slugs may be found throughout the marshes, east of Oserley. While you are hunting for the leader of the brigands, you might assist the people of Oserley by clearing the poisonous slugs out of the marshes.\n",
[9930]="700007B6\n1\tDefeat wights in the Great Barrow (total: 25)\tThe Great Barrow is at the southern end of the Barrow-downs. Bob Redthistle has asked you to enter the Great Barrow and keep more wights from getting out. He recommended that you take friends with you.\n2\tTalk to Bob Redthistle at Dead Man's Perch\tBob Redthistle awaits your return at Dead Man's Perch, between the north and south Barrow-downs. You should return to Bob Redthistle and let him know that you have destroyed many wights within the Great Barrow.\n",
[9931]="700173A8\n1\tSlay Ongbúrz Overmasters (total: 10)\tOngbúrz Overmasters can be found in the Library at Tham Mírdain, just to the south-west of Echad Mirobel. Hethugúr of Echad Mirobel has asked you to defeat Orc Overmasters at the Library, and to bring no more than a small handful of stout companions with you. The southern forces must not be alerted of your presence, so attacks against either side must be small and covert.\n",
[9932]="70006E14\n1\tDefeat Warg hunters (total: 4)\030Defeat dire Wargs (total: 4)\tDire Wargs roam the eastern plains of Nan Amlug. Warg hunters stalk the forests of western Nan Amlug. Mauno, the chief hunter of the Suuri-lehmä, has asked you to drive off the Wargs who are slaughtering the aurochs herds, threatening the Earth-kin's food supply.\n2\tTalk to Mauno\tMauno is at the camp of the Suuri-lehmä. Mauno, the chief hunter of the Suuri-lehmä, asked you to drive off the packs of Wargs which have been slaughtering the aurochs. There are many Wargs, but your efforts should make them more manageable. You should return to Mauno with news of your success.\n",
[9933]="70015674\n1\tDefeat the White Hand ambassadors (total: 3)\tThe White Hand ambassadors can be found within Skrithûrz-ulíma, a Moria Orc-encampment north-west of the Orc-watch. You should defeat White Hand ambassadors to prevent an alliance between Moria and Isengard.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have helped to thwart an alliance between Moria Orcs and Isengard.\n",
[9934]="7000135E\n1\tPour the tincture on the north monument\030Pour the tincture on the east monument\030Pour the tincture on the southern monument\tThe monuments are in Imlad Balchorth in front of the large lake. Oflár has asked you to bring the tincture to Imlad Balchorth and use it on the monuments to draw out the powerful spirits that guard them.\n2\tReturn the tincture to Oflár\tOflár is back at the dwarf-outpost of Myrkworth. You dispersed some fell spirits and slew the wights who came to defend the obelisk, but there was little other result. One wight boasted of something he called the Cauldron of Death. Oflár might know of these words.\n",
[9935]="7004CF82\n1\tFind Radagast\tRadagast can be found at the tree nursery just outside of Felegoth. Radagast the Brown has been asking after you. You should seek him out.\n2\tYou should examine the plant-life near the banks of the corrupted river Rhachló in hopes of discovering what still sickens the wood.\t\n3\tTalk to Oroniel near the Rhachló\tOroniel can be found by the northern banks of the Rhachló near Felegoth. You should present your findings to Oroniel.\n4\tExamine the sleeping Elf\030Examine the berries\030Examine the berry bush\tA sleeping Elf lies near Oroniel. You should examine the area and find out what has happened here.\n5\tTalk to Oroniel\tOroniel can be found by the northern banks of the Rhachló. You should speak to Oroniel about what you have learned.\n",
[9936]="70000C3D\n1\tDefeat trolls in Harloeg (total: 5)\tThe trolls dwell in a place called Harloeg, far to the south-east of the Tornstones. Trolls pursued the Earth-kin from the Ettenmoors far to the north-east and have taken residence in the far south-east corner of the Grimfens in the southern Lone-lands. Kekkonen, the Earth-kin chieftain, asked you to assist his people by destroying the trolls which pursued the fragile remnants of his people into the Lone-lands.\n2\tTalk to Kekkonen\tThe Earth-kin encampment is near the Tornstones, far to the north-west of Harloeg, south of the Great East Road. Return to the Earth-kin camp near the Tornstones and speak with Kekkonen. He waits to hear how you fared against the Trolls in the Grimfens.\n",
[9937]="70071D86\n1\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingar-garâsh when you are ready to go\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingar-garâsh when you are ready to go.\n2\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingar-garâsh\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingar-garâsh and report your success.\n",
[9938]="70071D87\n1\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingar-garâsh when you are ready to go\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingar-garâsh when you are ready to go.\n2\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingar-garâsh\tSpeak with Shâra Mizâdi in Ingar-garâsh.\n",
[9939]="70071D80\n1\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Zajâna\tSpeak with Mizâdi in Zajâna. Mizâdi said she intends to speak with the Doorwards, who can be found near the Shorakhúna, the great council hall in Zajâna.\n2\tFind Khâbakh within the Kalmakhíla in Zajâna\tFind Khâbakh within the Kalmakhíla to ask him for knowledge about the blight afflicting Adagím. The Kalmakhíla can be found on the western slope near the Khab Antâx within Zajâna.\n3\tReturn to Mizâdi outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna\tReturn to Mizâdi outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna.\n",
[9940]="70071D79\n1\tSpeak with Doorward Azagâya outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna\tSpeak with Doorward Azagâya outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna about rumours concerning Bârshud and his whereabouts.\n2\tSpeak with Muzâwi at the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna\tSpeak with Muzâwi at the Court of Larinâsta in Zajâna.\n3\tCollect herbs in the farming district of Zajâna (total: 12)\030Defeat street-rats in the farming district of Zajâna (total: 6)\tCollect herbs and defeat rats in the farming district of Zajâna.\n4\tReturn to Muzâwi in the Court of Larinâsta with the herbs\tReturn to Muzâwi in the Court of Larinâsta with the herbs and report your success.\n5\tReturn to speak with Mizâdi outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna\tReturn to speak with Mizâdi outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna with Muzâwi's report.\n",
[9941]="70071D72\n1\tSpeak with Doorward Azagâya outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna\tSpeak with Doorward Azagâya outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna about how to locate the Hall of Lajór in Zajâna.\n2\tEnter the area outside the Hall of Lajór in Zajâna\tEnter the area outside the Hall of Lajór in Zajâna. The Hall of Lajór can be found across the bridge and up the stairs from the Shorakhúna.\n3\tDefeat Ordâkhai outside the Hall of Lajór (total: 6)\tDefeat the Ordâkhai gathered outside the Hall of Lajór.\n4\tFind and interrogate Jórbol Bóro\030Find and interrogate Nirjára Bóro\030Find and interrogate Akráho Bóro\tFind and interrogate Jórbol Bóro, Nirjára Bóro, and Akráho Bóro outside the Hall of Lajór.\n5\tReturn to speak with Mizâdi outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna\tReturn to speak with Mizâdi outside the Shorakhúna in Zajâna with what information you have gathered.\n",
[9942]="70071574\n1\tSpeak with Elder Jurmêna in Sormedân about Khâbakh\tSpeak with Elder Jurmêna in Sormedân about the scholar Khâbakh. Sormedân can be found in Kighân to the west, within Mûr Ghala.\n",
[9943]="70041467\n1\tSearch for the Corsairs that fled Linhir\tThe Corsairs have likely fled into the hills to the north of Linhir. Garvir has asked you to seek out the Corsairs that fled during the recent attack on Linhir.\n2\tSearch the camp-site for Garvir's missing scout\tGarvir's scout can be found somewhere within Hata Khezrat in Dor-en-Ernil. You have discovered the Corsair encampment and should now seek out Garvir's scout.\n3\tGorroch can be found in Hata Khezrat in eastern Dor-en-Ernil. You have found Garvir's scout and should now free him from his bonds.\t\n4\tTalk to Gorroch\tGorroch can be found in Hata Khezrat to the north and slightly east of Linhir. You have freed Gorroch from his bonds and should now speak to him.\n",
[9944]="7000E83D\n1\tDefeat tomb-robbers in the Fields of Evendim (total: 15)\tTomb-robbers can be found throughout the eastern and north-easten regions of Evendim, far to the west of Esteldín. Handarod has asked you to defeat tomb-robbers in Evendim.\n2\tTalk to Handarod\tHandarod is at Esteldín, far to the east of Evendim. You should return to Handarod and tell him of your battles with the tomb-robbers.\n",
[9945]="7002FD05\n1\tDefeat Easterling snipers (total: 8)\tEasterling snipers can be found in Olghakhósh, the enemy encampment near Wakenflood on the banks of the Anduin. You should defeat a number of Easterling snipers, for they are deadly foes.\n2\tTalk to Sergeant Hubyrt\tSergeant Hubyrt can be found in Wakenflood. You should tell Sergeant Hubyrt of the Easterling snipers you defeated in Olghakhósh.\n",
[9946]="7001C493\n1\tDefeat wights in the ruins (total: 8)\tThere are wights in the ruins west of Ost Haer. Narthan believes that the time for absolution is close at hand and has asked you to mete justice out upon the wights infesting the ruins near Nindor and Ost Haer.\n2\tTalk to Narthan at Ost Haer\tNarthan is at Ost Haer in the southern bog of the Lone-lands. You combed through the ruins west of Ost Haer and destroyed many of the wights therein. Now you should return to Narthan.\n",
[9947]="70058786\n1\tComplete 'March on Gundabad: Assisting the War Effort' (total: 4)\tThe Gabil'akkâ, the Unified Army of Dwarves, has need of your assistance in the ongoing war effort. Complete 'March on Gundabad: Assisting the War Effort' several times to push forward the effort.\n2\tSpeak to Stálskeg Ironbeard\tYour assistance in completing several sorties for the Gabil'akkâ has been noted. Seek out Stálskeg Ironbeard and inform him of your deeds.\n",
[9948]="7000D4EE\n1\tDestroy crates in Bail Cátharnakh (total: 6)\tBail Cátharnakh is west of Gath Forthnír. Artain instructed you to destroy the food crates which the Trév Dúvardain are stockpiling for the Angmarim at Bail Cátharnakh.\n2\tTalk to Artain at Gath Forthnír\tArtain is at Gath Forthnír, east of Bail Cátharnakh. You should return to Artain and tell him of your success.\n",
[9949]="7003EA6E\n1\tDefeat bears in Nan Tornaeth (total: 6)\tThere are bears dwelling in Nan Tornaeth, in the Trollshaws. While in Nan Tornaeth, you should put down the maddened bears which dwell there, ending their suffering.\n",
[9950]="70068BB2\n1\tRetrieve surplus goods from outside the southern store-house (total: 4)\030Retrieve surplus goods from outside the western store-house (total: 4)\tSurplus goods can be found outside two store-houses located in the Fleet-fast.\n2\tBring the surplus goods to Nâjah in the Lower Ward\tNâjah is outside the entrance to the Fleet-fast from the Lower Ward.\n",
[9951]="700168B6\n1\tPress the first stone\tThe plaques are located in Balin's Camp in Nud-melek. The journal that Melkólf Stonecarver left behind contained the following puzzles: The journal reads: \"Dwarf who makes me has no need for me. Dwarf who buys me has no use for me. Dwarf who uses me would not want me.\" \"I have a hundred legs and cannot stand. I have no head and a long neck. I cannot see, but I am neat as can be.\" \"A hundred arms, a thousand fingers, And no eyes to see where it is I linger.\" \"With a knife, cut open my head, Then weep beside me when I am dead.\" \"I have no eyes, yet once did I see. I once had thoughts, now I'm empty.\" And then comes this strange little verse: \"Hundred-arms comes before headless long-neck. Head-cut-open is alone at the end. Headless long-neck comes after dwarf-and-me and hundred-arms. No-eyes comes after headless long-neck. Dwarf-and-me comes after hundred-arms\" The plaques associated with this puzzle are here in Balin's Camp!\n2\tPress the second stone\tThe journal reads: \"Dwarf who makes me has no need for me. Dwarf who buys me has no use for me. Dwarf who uses me would not want me.\" \"I have a hundred legs and cannot stand. I have no head and a long neck. I cannot see, but I am neat as can be.\" \"A hundred arms, a thousand fingers, And no eyes to see where it is I linger.\" \"With a knife, cut open my head, Then weep beside me when I am dead.\" \"I have no eyes, yet once did I see. I once had thoughts, now I'm empty.\" And then comes this strange little verse: \"Hundred-arms comes before headless long-neck. Head-cut-open is alone at the end. Headless long-neck comes after dwarf-and-me and hundred-arms. No-eyes comes after headless long-neck. Dwarf-and-me comes after hundred-arms\" The plaques associated with this puzzle are here in Balin's Camp!\n3\tPress the third stone\tThe journal reads: \"Dwarf who makes me has no need for me. Dwarf who buys me has no use for me. Dwarf who uses me would not want me.\" \"I have a hundred legs and cannot stand. I have no head and a long neck. I cannot see, but I am neat as can be.\" \"A hundred arms, a thousand fingers, And no eyes to see where it is I linger.\" \"With a knife, cut open my head, Then weep beside me when I am dead.\" \"I have no eyes, yet once did I see. I once had thoughts, now I'm empty.\" And then comes this strange little verse: \"Hundred-arms comes before headless long-neck. Head-cut-open is alone at the end. Headless long-neck comes after dwarf-and-me and hundred-arms. No-eyes comes after headless long-neck. Dwarf-and-me comes after hundred-arms\" The plaques associated with this puzzle are here in Balin's Camp!\n4\tPress the fourth stone\tThe journal reads: \"Dwarf who makes me has no need for me. Dwarf who buys me has no use for me. Dwarf who uses me would not want me.\" \"I have a hundred legs and cannot stand. I have no head and a long neck. I cannot see, but I am neat as can be.\" \"A hundred arms, a thousand fingers, And no eyes to see where it is I linger.\" \"With a knife, cut open my head, Then weep beside me when I am dead.\" \"I have no eyes, yet once did I see. I once had thoughts, now I'm empty.\" And then comes this strange little verse: \"Hundred-arms comes before headless long-neck. Head-cut-open is alone at the end. Headless long-neck comes after dwarf-and-me and hundred-arms. No-eyes comes after headless long-neck. Dwarf-and-me comes after hundred-arms\" The plaques associated with this puzzle are here in Balin's Camp!\n5\tPress the fifth stone\tThe journal reads: \"Dwarf who makes me has no need for me. Dwarf who buys me has no use for me. Dwarf who uses me would not want me.\" \"I have a hundred legs and cannot stand. I have no head and a long neck. I cannot see, but I am neat as can be.\" \"A hundred arms, a thousand fingers, And no eyes to see where it is I linger.\" \"With a knife, cut open my head, Then weep beside me when I am dead.\" \"I have no eyes, yet once did I see. I once had thoughts, now I'm empty.\" And then comes this strange little verse: \"Hundred-arms comes before headless long-neck. Head-cut-open is alone at the end. Headless long-neck comes after dwarf-and-me and hundred-arms. No-eyes comes after headless long-neck. Dwarf-and-me comes after hundred-arms\" The plaques associated with this puzzle are here in Balin's Camp!\n6\tCompleted\tYou have solved the puzzle of the carvings!\n",
[9952]="7005A952\n1\tLocate the lit moon mirror\tA lit moon mirror must be somewhere in Máttugard. You should locate the lit moon mirror.\n2\tReposition the lit moon mirror\tA lit moon mirror must be somewhere in Máttugard. You should reposition the lit moon mirror.\n3\tReposition a second moon mirror\tAnother moon mirror must be somewhere else in Máttugard. You should reposition a second moon mirror.\n4\tReposition a third moon mirror\tAnother moon mirror must be somewhere else in Máttugard. You should reposition a third moon mirror.\n5\tReturn to the Plaque of the Moon\tThe Plaque of the Moon can be found in Máttugard. You should return to the Plaque of the Moon.\n6\tFind the first plaque\tA first plaque must be somewhere in Máttugard. You should find the first plaque. 'By night, the moon reflects in my waters. 'The nobles walk by at all hours. 'Each day, you converse around me.'\n7\tFind the second plaque\tA second plaque must be somewhere in Máttugard. You should find the second plaque. 'By night, the moon reflects in my waters. 'The nobles walk by at all hours. 'Each day, you converse around me.'\n8\tFind the third plaque\tA third plaque must be somewhere in Máttugard. You should find the third plaque. 'By night, the moon reflects in my waters. 'The nobles walk by at all hours. 'Each day, you converse around me.'\n9\tReturn to the Plaque of the Moon\tThe Plaque of the Moon can be found in Máttugard. You should return to the Plaque of the Moon.\n",
})
